abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proof that the maximum over [0, T] of a constructed Airy_1 process,
  centred and scaled as in the paper, converges to the Gumbel law as T tends
  to infinity, assuming three named inputs: the finite-dimensional Airy_1
  laws, a cubic GOE left-tail bound, and cubic strong mixing. The mesoscopic
  step uses a two-time Fredholm determinant bound instead of the paper's
  association and covariance argument. The two-term tail expansion over a
  fixed interval (Proposition 1.2) is proved for the constructed process for
  every positive length under the first two inputs. The two-interval
  determinant formula (Lemma 3.1, in the trace-class form of Remark 3.2) is
  proved for every equal positive length under the same two inputs. The
  block modulus estimate (Lemma 4.1) is proved under the same two inputs and
  a fourth named input, the transferred local oscillation bound (4.2) on
  windows inside [0, infinity), which is assumed, not proved; the main
  theorem does not use it. The threshold-sensitive Newman bound (Lemma 4.2)
  is proved under the first two inputs and the association of the Airy_1
  process (ProcessAssociated, Pu 2025), which is assumed, not proved; the
  main theorem does not use it either. The mesoscopic sum (Proposition 4.3)
  is proved under the first two inputs and three named inputs, each assumed,
  not proved: the bound (4.2), the association of the Airy_1 process, and
  the covariance asymptotic of the Airy_1 process (CubicCovarianceDecay,
  Basu-Busani-Ferrari 2023); the main theorem uses none of them. Remark 5.3
  (the Gumbel limit along integer lengths from the Ferrari-Liu persistence
  estimates) is proved under the first two inputs and a new named input,
  the finite-length persistence expansion of Ferrari-Liu 2024
  (FerrariLiuPersistence), which is assumed, not proved, and used only
  there. The first input is proved under the second (not unconditionally),
  through flat discrete TASEP and its scaling limit, so the main theorem
  also holds under the second and third inputs alone. Since v0.10.0 the
  first two inputs are theorems: the cubic GOE left tail is proved with no
  hypothesis (by Hermite localization of the GOE kernel operator), and with
  it the first input, so the main theorem also holds under cubic strong
  mixing only. The comparator checks that one-input form, the two proved
  inputs, the two-input form, the proof of the first input from the second
  and the original statements, which are unchanged and still take the
  first two inputs as hypotheses; no input is added. This checks the paper's main theorem along that route and the listed component
  results; it does not certify the whole manuscript.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Airy process
  - KPZ universality
  - extreme value theory
  - Gumbel distribution
  - Fredholm determinant
  - formal verification
